  <title>Shipping info</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>General</gui><gui>Shipping info</gui></guiseq> records a
  parcel sent to a contact, with its tracking number, pays the carrier for it,
  and can charge the freight to the customer's invoice, all in one go.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>On the <gui>Shipping</gui> tab, choose the
    <gui>Contact</gui>. Their earlier shipments are listed under
    <gui>Customer shipping history</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Invoice</gui> the parcel's goods are on, and/or
    type a <gui>Description</gui> of what was sent.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the <gui>Tracking number</gui> and check the
    <gui>Date</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>To charge the freight to the invoice, leave <gui>Freight
    product</gui> checked and choose the product freight is billed as. The
    product is remembered for next time. Clear the check to record the
    shipment without charging the customer this time.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Payment</gui>. The <gui>Payment</gui> tab is the
    carrier's bill; fill it in and pay it as in <link
    xref="incoming_invoice"/>.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>When the carrier's bill is saved, the shipment is recorded and, if
  freight is being charged, the amount paid is added to the invoice as one line
  of the freight product, with the tracking number as its remark. An invoice
  window open on that invoice reloads.</p>

  <section id="which_invoices">
  <title>Which invoices can be charged</title>
  <p>Only invoices that are not paid, not cancelled, not yet on a statement and
  not already shipped are listed: an invoice carries one shipment. If the
  invoice has already been posted, you are asked to confirm, because it has
  probably been sent to the customer. When the chosen invoice cannot take the
  charge, the <gui>Freight product</gui> row is greyed out. To record a
  shipment for any other reason, type a <gui>Description</gui> and leave the
  invoice empty.</p>
  </section>

  <p><gui>Shipping history</gui> opens <link xref="shipping_history"/>.</p>

